@* One turn of a repeat: what was asked, the tool calls folded away with each input and result, the answer as the
   agent sent it, the agent's error when it ended in one, and the turn's marks, two to a row on a wide screen, each
   criterion with its Flip. *@

<section class="card-p turn-card">
    <h2>Turn @Number</h2>
    <p class="turn-ask">@Turn.Transcript.Ask</p>

    @if (Turn.Transcript.Calls.Count > 0)
    {
        <details class="turn-calls">
            <summary>@CallsSummary</summary>
            @foreach (var call in Turn.Transcript.Calls)
            {
                <div class="turn-call">
                    <div class="turn-call-tool">@call.Tool</div>
                    <pre class="turn-call-input">@call.Input</pre>
                    <pre class="turn-call-result">@call.Result</pre>
                </div>
            }
        </details>
    }

    <blockquote class="turn-answer">@Turn.Transcript.Answer</blockquote>
    <p class="turn-costs">@AgentCostName @AgentCost · @JudgeCostName @JudgeCost</p>

    @if (Turn.Transcript.Error is { } error)
    {
        <p class="turn-error"><strong>The agent's error</strong> @error</p>
    }

    <div class="turn-marks row g-3">
        @foreach (var fact in Turn.Facts)
        {
            <div class="col-12 col-lg-6"><MarkLine Mark="fact" Kind="MarkKind.Fact"/></div>
        }
        @foreach (var (criterion, number) in Turn.Criteria.Select((criterion, at) => (criterion, at + 1)))
        {
            <div class="col-12 col-lg-6"><MarkLine Mark="criterion" Kind="MarkKind.Criterion" Place="PlaceOf(number)" OnFlip="OnFlip" OnUndo="OnUndo"/></div>
        }
    </div>
</section>
